A person asked their assistant a question. The assistant holds the saved facts below, which the person told it earlier.
Question: which ONE saved fact is about the thing or person the question asks about, in whatever words?
Answer {"answer": N} with the number of that fact.
Answer {"answer": 0} when none of them is: a fact about a DIFFERENT thing or person of a similar kind (another machine, another relative, another place) is not it, and most questions are about nothing saved.

Asked: "who looks after my teeth?" Saved facts: 1. "my bike lock code is 4471." 2. "Dr Ferro is my dentist." 3. "we rent the same cottage on Skye every August." -> {"answer": 2}
Asked: "when is my sister's birthday?" Saved facts: 1. "my brother's birthday is 2 June." 2. "coffee after 3 pm keeps me awake all night." -> {"answer": 0}
Asked: "what speed is the liquidiser on?" Saved facts: 1. "my coffee grinder is on speed 2." 2. "my blender is on speed 5." -> {"answer": 2}
Asked: "how tall is Mount Etna?" Saved facts: 1. "my running shoes are size 44." -> {"answer": 0}

Asked: "who sees my pet when shes poorly?" Saved facts:
1. "my vet for the cat is Dr Okonkwo."
Reply with ONLY the JSON object: {"answer": N}

A person said one sentence to their assistant in passing. They did not ask for it to be remembered.
Question: does the sentence tell a lasting fact about the person's PRIVATE life?
Answer {"answer": "yes"} only when it is about their home and belongings and where those are kept or go, their family, friends, neighbours or pets, their health and body, what they eat and drink, their habits and routines, or a standing arrangement in their personal life, and it will still be true next month. It counts even with no "I" or "my" in it.
Answer {"answer": "no"} when it is about work or a project (code, builds, systems, files, documents, drafts, charts, clients, suppliers, deadlines, meetings), about this conversation, about the world at large or general knowledge, about today's mood, weather, traffic or a one-off event, or something imagined.

Said: "the spare duvet lives in the top of the hall cupboard." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "the export job timed out twice on the staging box." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "our neighbour Petra feeds the cat when we are away." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "that last paragraph reads much better than the first draft." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "the bike with the red frame is Jonas's, mine is the grey one." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "the supplier pushed the delivery date to next week." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "peppermint tea settles me after a long shift." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "bees can recognise human faces." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "the gate at the allotment sticks unless you lift it." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "the report template looks fine now." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "ugh, the wifi dropped twice during that call." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "suppose the train were cancelled and we had to drive." -> {"answer": "no"}

Said: "im thinking of visiting her next month" ->
Reply with ONLY the JSON object: {"answer": "yes"} or {"answer": "no"}

A person said one sentence to their assistant.
Question: is the person TELLING the assistant how something in their life is?
Answer {"answer": "yes"} when the sentence states a fact that already holds: how something is, where something is kept, who someone is, what suits them, or what they or others regularly do.
Answer {"answer": "no"} when the sentence asks or tells the assistant to DO something (a task: change, move, name, sort, find, make or send something), with or without "please".
Answer {"answer": "no"} when the sentence is about something that has not happened and is not settled: something the person will probably, may, might or could do some time, is thinking of, would like, or has not decided.

Said: "the spare duvet lives in the top of the hall cupboard." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "turn the scanned receipt the right way up for me." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "our neighbour Petra feeds the cat when we are away." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "I'm tempted to take up pottery in the autumn." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "we go to my mother's for Christmas every year." -> {"answer": "yes"}
Said: "copy the wedding pictures onto the stick so gran can have them." -> {"answer": "no"}
Said: "peppermint tea settles me after a long shift." -> {"answer": "yes"}
